{"nodes": [{"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_heterologous_review_dual_track", "label": "D-013 Dual-Track Review: real heterologous wh-review + independent subagent, unavailable recorded honestly", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1118-L1126, L1263", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PRD rounds four and five demonstrated the two review forms are not interchangeable, so both are required and recorded separately; provider unavailability is recorded as unavailable/partial and never converted into a pass."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_context_discipline_subagents", "label": "D-015 Execution Discipline: heavy re-reads run in subagents, main session receives summaries only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1138-L1145, L1314", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "None of the original 22 open items carried this user requirement, so a review finding forced adding OI-23 as its carrier; the record must show actor, command, exit_code and conclusion summary, without introducing any new persistent object."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_constitution_version_bump", "label": "D-016 Constitution 1.8.0 -> 1.9.0, still 22 articles, wording shown to the user first", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1147-L1155, L1315", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "CONSTITUTION.md:187 mandates a four-part synchronisation on any content change; machine guards hard-check the article count at 22, so new paragraphs must not become a 23rd article. Wording is treated as a user-visible commitment and therefore previewed before it is written."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_zero_new_control_plane_non_goals", "label": "Non-goals: no new control plane, no historical-byte edits, no host fixes, no re-running real tasks", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L563-L564, L706-L717, L770", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Historical bytes' is precisely limited to test/review/provenance/completed-task evidence, while this task group's upstream planning materials (the parent decision log and PRD) are treated as live and may be corrected. The screening found none of the four fixes needs a new persistent object, field, state literal, gate or file; if one ever can only be fixed by adding a state literal or field, it stops there and is recorded incomplete rather than silently expanding authority."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_build_spec_hard_constraints", "label": "Three Hard Constraints on build-spec (no new fields/schemas/literals, log test changes, writer-side acceptance)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L698-L702", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Written hard so the implementation may not relax them on its own: the frozen STAGE_ROW_KEYS table forbids new row fields, the two test expectations that flip must be registered rather than loosened, and blocker 1's acceptance rests on writer-side repair plus a narrow regression test plus honest registration of the historical bad row (later replacing the earlier on-site read-back requirement)."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_unknown_unavailable_discipline", "label": "Honesty Discipline: unknown / unavailable / partial are recorded as facts, never rewritten as passes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1319, L1365-L1369, L1419-L1424", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Applied concretely: review round two returned MATERIAL_FORBIDDEN for both roles because the sender projected a summary instead of the contract's required materials, and the record keeps that as an unavailable fact with no findings rather than as a clean result; the missing session-bound stage outcome, stage-end spec-analyze and reflection all share one root cause (no host-recorded session transcript) and stay unavailable/missing."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_finding_disposition_record", "label": "Finding Disposition Record (25 runtime dispositions: 23 fixed / 2 rejected_invalid)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1288-L1325, L1421", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every finding id is enumerated with its disposition and basis; the third round's report file contains only the pairing JSON without finding bodies, so the full findings live in the results files, and the red/blue count discrepancy (21+12 reported vs 20+12 summarised) is logged rather than smoothed over."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_c7_c8_acceptance_criteria", "label": "C7 13 AC + C8 9 AC, each with pass criterion, oracle command and failure criterion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1199-L1231", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_c7_ac13_scope_correction", "label": "C7-AC-13 Correction: code-side change surface = close convergence + 5 runtime files + package.json + CI", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1217, L1293", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two blocking review findings caught that the upstream AC's 'code-side change is exactly the operations/close surface' contradicted the already-approved scope; the record corrects the AC rather than the scope and registers the discrepancy as 'upstream AC conflicts with approved scope, corrected per confirmed decision'."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_decision_hash_two_readings", "label": "decision_hash Two Readings (bound-at-confirmation value vs current file value)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1214, L1341", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Confirmation binds the file's byte state after the user's reply line; both readings must be stated explicitly so they are not mixed."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_oi_outline_v1", "label": "OI Outline v1 (24 open items, 6 framework nodes, 6 fixed categories)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L93-L180", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recorded twice on purpose: the human-readable table in the body and the fenced YAML block are the same records with the same oi_id, because the existing analyzer analyzeDecisionOutline reads only the fenced block; writing two divergent sets is forbidden by the material's own contract."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_stage_row_key_freeze", "label": "Frozen 16-Key Stage Row Field Table (STAGE_ROW_KEYS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L693, L712", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exact-key check throws when the key set differs from the frozen table, which is precisely why 'add a material_scope field' was never an option and why several candidate fixes are constrained to rewriting write-side or read-side logic."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_c5_semantic_reconciliation", "label": "C5 Semantic Reconciliation: read-side stale rejection was deleted by design in task II", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1511-L1526", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two verify-code major findings were rejected as 'by design' because task II explicitly deleted B-class freshness/currentness comparison and automatic re-run, and approved that stale facts stay readable after material edits; restoring a read-side stale gate would break named C5 tests, so the finding is recorded as a design reconciliation rather than a defect."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_handoff_failure_execution_fact", "label": "F-c57aff1d9c2c handoff-failure fix: implementation_completion must follow handoff published+current", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1528-L1539", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "REAL major bug: a failed stage-handoff could still write implementation_completion=completed while evidence showed exit_code=1 and execution_outcome=incomplete. Fixed so only a published-and-current handoff writes completed; quality semantics are untouched because execution failure is disclosed through the execution layer rather than becoming a quality gate, preserving the four-layer independence rule. RED before / GREEN after evidence is recorded."}, {"id": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_m4_net_subtraction_line", "label": "D-012 M4 = combined net-negative across task I+II+III merge commits", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L1106-L1116, L1225", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measuring only task III could force deleting things just to make the number negative, while the C7 card itself admits governance text is the one legitimate net increase; so M4 spans the whole remediation line and a positive single task must state its reason. Link-level acceptance reuses this task's own materials and store instead of spawning a real task, which would violate C8-FR-10."}], "edges": [{"source": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_decision_log", "target": "specs_archive_workflowhub_mechanism_simplification_t3_20260912_decision_log_oi_outline_v1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "specs/archive/workflowhub-mechanism-simplification-t3-20260912/decision-log.md", "source_location": "L93-L180", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "specs_ar